The worst of it is, this one is probably a feature, not a bug.

I had bones files for level 4, 5, 6, & 7, and had really littered level 4
with ghosts, aggravated pets, Kops, and a lady shopkeeper with a mad glint
in her eye.  I'd lost, in other words, half a dozen explorers trying to
survive "the crowd at the foot of the stairs".

This time, I took two tame pets, fed another immediately when I arrived
on level four, and the four of us were battling the Kops with fair results
when the shopkeepress bullied her way through the crowd to my side.  Though
I tried to pay the bill of some prior miscreant who had robbed her shop, I
didn't have the pelf, and the lady was out for "blood, not money".  About
this time, I pretty much simultaneously caught a cream pie in the puss,
tried to #wipe it, saw my hit points plummit, panicked back to the top of
the stairs (level three), got brutally murdered by a stair vaulting clerk
for a crime I didn't commit, and died unremembered.

And without _any_ bones files left!

I _know_ the rule is "die on level three or above, you don't have any chance
of getting a bones file created", but should that wipe out existing bones
files on levels I haven't even _reached_ yet? I'd like to whine and whimper
a bit about how dreadfully unfair life is, but nobody told me the dungeon
was going to be easy.

The environment is an Amiga 2000 running 3.09i, and I think this relates
to seeing all my bones files' timestamps updated after every game.

Come on, dev team, have a heart!  Please decouple the bones files again,
so they get retained or removed sensibly in this admittedly rare
circumstance.

;-)

